cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Dietary Creatine Intake and Depression in U.S. Adults: a Multi-Cycle NHANES Replication and Sensitivity Analysis of Bakian 2020"
authors:
  - family-names: "Piñero Roig"
    given-names: "Laura"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-3390-4029"
    affiliation: "Universitat de Barcelona, Faculty of Medicine"
abstract: >-
  Secondary analysis of NHANES 2013-March 2020 extending Bakian et al.
  2020 on dietary creatine intake and depression risk. The association
  replicates only once seafood is counted as a source of creatine: the
  same survey-weighted model is re-run under four exposure definitions,
  and Q4 vs Q1 moves from 0.81 (0.60-1.07) to 0.72 (0.54-0.95). A spline
  dose-response model and a formal interaction test with antidepressant
  medication use are reported alongside it. Implemented in R with the
  survey package. Presented as an oral communication at the 5th IJMS
  World Conference of Medical Student Research, July 2026.
repository-code: "https://github.com/laurapiro17/wcmsr-creatine-nhanes"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - NHANES
  - nutritional epidemiology
  - depression
  - creatine
  - restricted cubic splines
  - survey statistics
  - clinical research
date-released: 2026-04-29
